# A One Master Prompt — Implementation Phases

## Phase 1 — DONE (foundation)
- Customer Persona schema (`customerPersonaSchema.js`)
- Tenant scope defaults (`tenantScope.js`)
- Customer repository layer (`repositories/customerRepository.js`)
- Persona service (`services/customerPersonaService.js`)
- Hooks: bill submit, F8 identity, manager payment, cashier payment reconcile, returns

## Phase 2 — DONE (incremental, safe)
- Admin `CustomersControl.jsx` + manager `Customers.jsx` → `customerAdminService` (no direct Firestore)
- Biller customer cache reads → `customerRepository` + `orderRepository`
- `tenantId` in Firestore rules (`customers`) + setup wizard flag
- Persona offline queue via `sync_queue` (`customer:merge` in syncWorker)
- Credit transaction → `creditHistory` append on bill/payment persona patches

## Phase 3 — DONE (architecture stubs)
- Repository stubs: `orderRepository`, `paymentRepository`, `expenseRepository`, `inventoryRepository`
- ESLint warn: pages must not import `firebase/firestore` or heavy firebase exports
- Dashboard stats → `dashboardStatsService` (summary docs first)

## Phase 4 — OUT OF SCOPE (current phase)
- Business Hub
- WhatsApp Hub
- Heavy AI / historical analytics inside Operational POS

## Remaining incremental (optional, not blocking)
- Migrate remaining admin pages (Bills, Reports, Cashier, Biller core) to repositories gradually
- Full `tenantId` enforcement on orders/payments/expenses rules
- Cloud Function daily summary writes (client read-only today)

When implementing, preserve stable billing/cashier modules unless explicitly requested.
